# GoodEnough Project Rule

Before changing this repository, read `CURSOR_HANDOFF.md` and the source-of-truth files it lists.

- Work on branch `codex/goodenough-day0`, not `main`.
- Preserve existing uncommitted changes and never expose or stage `.env`.
- Follow the approved implementation plan task by task using tests first.
- Briefly explain each concept immediately before implementing it.
- Keep the strict three-week deadline and apply the documented cut order.
- Do not add a dashboard, model, dataset, learned router, streaming, or unrelated abstraction.
- Keep semantic prompts identical across deployments; deployment controls remain outside prompt text.
- Do not run benchmark calls until the pre-registration amendment and frozen split manifest are committed.
- Do not tune prompts or parsers using map or router results.
- Preserve raw responses, errors, item membership, and statistical uncertainty.
- Never use em dashes in project prose.

Current execution target: Task 1 in `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-31-goodenough-day0-implementation-plan.md`.
